-- ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
-- Update test_results biomarker_id Foreign Key On Delete Behavior
-- Created: 2026-02-15
-- Purpose: Allow deletion of biomarkers from mastertable by setting references to NULL
-- ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

DO $$ 
BEGIN
    -- 1. Drop the existing constraint if it exists
    -- The name test_results_biomarker_id_fkey is the default generated by Postgres
    ALTER TABLE public.test_results 
    DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS test_results_biomarker_id_fkey;

    -- 2. Re-add the constraint with ON DELETE SET NULL
    -- SET NULL is used for test_results to preserve historical user data 
    -- even if the master biomarker definition is removed.
    ALTER TABLE public.test_results
    ADD CONSTRAINT test_results_biomarker_id_fkey 
    FOREIGN KEY (biomarker_id) 
    REFERENCES public.biomarkers_mastertable(biomarker_id) 
    ON DELETE SET NULL;

    -- 3. Also handle biomarkers_aliases if it exists
    -- CASCADE is used here because aliases are meaningless without the master record.
    IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_name = 'biomarkers_aliases') THEN
        ALTER TABLE public.biomarkers_aliases 
        DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS biomarkers_aliases_biomarker_id_fkey;
        
        ALTER TABLE public.biomarkers_aliases
        ADD CONSTRAINT biomarkers_aliases_biomarker_id_fkey 
        FOREIGN KEY (biomarker_id) 
        REFERENCES public.biomarkers_mastertable(biomarker_id) 
        ON DELETE CASCADE;
    END IF;

END $$;
